<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified" version="2.0">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
RESPONSE schema for couponPost (Customer360). Returned in the response body.
Audited 2026-10-12 against the loyalty-app service generation.

Two document roots are possible:
  1. WEBSERVICE/RESPONSE -- every response produced by the operation itself.
  2. bare RESPONSE       -- produced before the operation runs (access-token gate, E899) or by
                            the generic runtime-error page (E999).

How to read the outcome:
  - SUCCESS is RESPONSE_CODE S104 together with RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_AVAILABLE. The coupon
    has been consumed (marked as scanned) by this call.
  - Any other RESPONSE_CODE means nothing was posted.

RESPONSE_CODE catalog (kept as xs:string on purpose; new codes must not break validation):
  S104 coupon posted (success)
  E101 XmlInput empty       E102 malformed XML      E103 parser configuration   E104 I/O reading input
       (E101-E104 are emitted as a child of WEBSERVICE, AFTER an empty RESPONSE element)
  E113 promotion is not assigned to the requesting store (RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E115 no store could be resolved
  E116 REQ_COUPON_CODE missing or empty
  E117 coupon already reconciled against an order (RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_AUDITED)
  E118 coupon already scanned (RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_REDEEMED)
  E119 the coupon's promotion is not approved or has ended (RESP_STATUS_CODE PROMO_UNAVAILABLE)
  E123 coupon expired, or not yet valid (RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E127 REQ_STORE_ID unknown
  E841 coupon code not found (COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E842 REQ_COUPON_TYPE missing or different from the promotion's type (RESP_STATUS_CODE empty)
  E843 coupon usage limit reached (COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E855 CUSTOMER_ID supplied but not a known customer
  E899 accessTokenKey validation failed (bare RESPONSE root)
  E999 unhandled error (bare RESPONSE root, empty RESPONSE_DATE, no ResponseId)
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Top-level wrapper for every response produced by the couponPost operation.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Response payload. Echoes the posted coupon and reports the post outcome. Empty (attribute only) on E101-E104 and when the request contained no REQUEST element.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_DETAILS" minOccurs="0">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Echo of the coupon that was posted.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:sequence>
                    <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_CODE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The coupon code exactly as sent in REQ_COUPON_CODE (including any tenant prefix). Empty when no code was sent (E116).</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_TYPE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Echo of REQ_COUPON_TYPE as sent (SERIALIZE or NONSERIALIZE; may be empty). Emitted on success and on E113, E117, E118, E119, E841, E842, E843 and on E123 when the coupon has expired; absent on E115, E116, E127, E855 and on E123 when the coupon is not yet valid.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:sequence>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
              <!-- NOTE: 'TRANSACTOIN' is a genuine misspelling in the service and is the ONLY spelling emitted. Do NOT correct it; it is the real wire contract. -->
              <xs:element name="RESP_TRANSACTOIN_DETAILS" minOccurs="0">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Outcome of the coupon post. Modeled as a repeating choice: RESP_STATUS_CODE is not returned with every code.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                    <xs:element name="RESP_STATUS_CODE" type="xs:string">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Status of the coupon. Values emitted: COUPON_AVAILABLE (with S104: the coupon was valid and has now been posted); COUPON_AUDITED (with E117); COUPON_REDEEMED (with E118); COUPON_UNAVAILABLE (with E113, E123, E841, E843); PROMO_UNAVAILABLE (with E119); EMPTY (with E842). Absent on E115, E116, E127, E855.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Outcome code. S104 on success; see the catalog in the schema header.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:choice>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Present here only on the gate-error envelope of the older service generation (E888 / E899): RESPONSE then carries this element alone.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
              </xs:element>
            </xs:sequence>
            <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>Request-log correlation id generated by the service for this call. Quote it when reporting an issue.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:attribute>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Input-level failure code E101-E104 only. These four codes are emitted here, as a child of WEBSERVICE following an empty RESPONSE element, not inside RESP_TRANSACTOIN_DETAILS.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Bare RESPONSE root (no WEBSERVICE wrapper). Used only for failures raised outside the operation: E899 (accessTokenKey validation failed; carries ResponseId and a RESPONSE_DATE timestamp) and E999 (unhandled error; RESPONSE_DATE is an EMPTY element and there is no ResponseId).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Server timestamp "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" (e.g. 2026-10-12 15:00:02.123) on E899; empty on E999. Deliberately xs:string: the format is not ISO 8601.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>E899 or E999.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Request-log correlation id. Present on E899; absent on E999.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
